elp  you survive which is your sole means of  gaining ground  you're pitched struggle some of the  underlying problems of the PC version of  don't starve waiter on the ps4 don't  starves roguelike aspect is utterly  grueling in the way it doles out  punishment while there are a few limited  means to prolong your life beyond the  grave most games that end with you dying  wipe out your progress completely this  leaves you agonizing over the numerous  hours you just spent chipping away to  gain a foothold your experience carries  over and goes towards unlocking new  characters with special perks to play as  so it's not a total loss but there's a  special kind of agony of having to grind  through from the beginning after getting  killed in a later game run if you're up  to the challenge and precariousness of  exploring the stark landscape bristling  with danger don't starve delivers  exhaustive depth and brutal punishments  in equal measure  it's grindy and frustrating at times but  it's also a beautifully grim experience  that controls nicely and packs an  absorbing punch  [Music]

